The five points that can touch Black on the first move are A1,A3,A4,B1,B2.

* W A1 is met by B B1 and the white stone is captured at once, the B1 stone connecting C1-C2. W A3 is immediately in atari on A4 and is captured at once by B A4. W A4 is met by B A3 and is reduced to the single liberty A5.

* W B1 puts C1-C2 in atari on B2 and puts W B1 itself in atari on A1. The only legal reply that keeps C1-C2 alive is B B2. B B2 joins A2,B3-B4,C1-C2 into one group with the three effective liberties A1,A3,A4 and W B1 now lives only on A1. B A1 captures W B1 and the merged black group is never reduced to zero liberties. W A1 after the connection is suicide.

* W B2 puts C1-C2 in atari on B1 and puts W B2 itself in atari on B1. Black is forced B B1, which captures W B2 and leaves

A2 {A1,A3,B2}
B3-B4 {A3,A4,B2}
C1-C2-B1 {A1,B2}

with B2 empty again after the capture. A1 is suicide for White against A2+B1 and B2 is suicide for White against A2+B1+B3+C2. The only legal White continuations are A3 or A4. A3 is in atari on A4 and is captured at once by B A4, A4 is met by a Black defence that keeps the left side on A1,A3,B2 and allows Black to recapture or regain liberty A4. No Black group is ever forced to zero liberties and White never obtains a forced capturing net.

Hence under orthodox liberty/suicide rules no first White move initiates a plan of White moves against which Black has no defence that keeps at least one of its groups alive. The set of winning first moves is empty.

